WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.859
OK, Donald Trump, again, is saying that Corona
virus is dying out and it's just going to

00:00:06.859 --> 00:00:07.979
go away.

00:00:07.979 --> 00:00:12.970
Donald Trump was interviewed yesterday about
his upcoming rally in Tulsa, Oklahoma.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.150
Disastrous idea.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.180
Dr. Anthony Foushee says, I wouldn't go to
any large events, including this rally.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:23.210
Just not a good idea and not a smart idea
as a pandemic is still continuing to rage.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:27.930
Donald Trump said now the rally is fine because
Corona virus is dying out.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:32.279
Coronavirus cases are rising in 22 states,
including Oklahoma, where you plan to hold

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:33.279
a big rally this week.

00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:35.240
Aren't you afraid about people getting sick?

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:40.170
No, because if you look, the numbers are very
minuscule compared to what it was.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.170
It's dying out.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:44.510
By the way, we're doing very well in vaccines
and therapeutics also.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:48.710
I think there's going to be some big announcements
on that in the not too distant future.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:50.260
But no, we're not concerned.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:54.300
Actually, Oklahoma has had a very low rate,
relatively speaking.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.990
It is a little spike, a small spike for a
specific reason.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:58.990
But no.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.510
We had over a million people apply.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.990
They have people now days ahead, lined up.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.610
They have big lines of people.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.760
So Trump said the numbers are minuscule.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.600
The numbers are not minuscule.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.920
We were at one point seeing 30000 new cases
a day.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:18.580
We are now seeing 23000 new cases a day.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.760
That's not minuscule.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:25.060
As I've already told you a bunch of times
this week, many states are seeing record spikes.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.850
Texas, Florida, Arizona, etc.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:35.700
We have more than 20000 new cases every single
day, people being diagnosed with Corona virus.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.890
But there is something that is truly chilling
about Donald Trump saying it will eventually

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.730
go away.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.000
Eventually it will go away.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:51.470
And his followers are so ignorant and so desperate
for Donald Trump to be right that Trump, in

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:52.910
a sense, is correct.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:57.710
It will eventually go away and his followers
are just ignorant enough that they might give

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:01.620
him the credit for it or at least say, look,
Trump was right all along.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.330
Now, let me explain what I mean by that.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:07.310
Eventually, even without a vaccine.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:10.840
Eventually, if the virus keeps spreading and
spreading and spreading.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.260
You're going to get to 70 percent of the country
getting the virus.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:20.411
And that is the threshold that is believed
to be the threshold for herd immunity, for

00:02:20.411 --> 00:02:24.420
something that is contagious to the degree
that corona virus is contagious.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:27.510
Now, this is important to understand.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:32.260
Herd immunity is not a fixed number for a
more contagious disease.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.530
You need a higher percentage of immunity to
get to herd immunity.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:43.599
So measles is so contagious that the estimates
are you need 95 percent immunity to have herd

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:44.910
immunity.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:50.160
Corona virus is less contagious, as far as
we know, than measles dramatically so.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.650
And so it is estimated that you need about
70 percent immunity.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:57.740
Now, that could be a combination of vaccinations
and people who got and recovered from the

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:58.740
disease.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.740
We don't have a vaccination right now.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:04.849
So in order to get the 70 percent we would
have of three hundred and thirty million Americans.

00:03:04.849 --> 00:03:09.940
Two hundred and thirty million would be infected
with a roughly point seven percent infection

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.060
fatality rate.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.490
That means about one point six million people
would die.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:16.569
So Trump is right.

00:03:16.569 --> 00:03:20.739
Eventually it will die out because so many
people will have gotten it that somewhere

00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:25.470
around a million and a half will have died
and we will have herd immunity.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:28.310
That doesn't mean Trump is handling this correctly.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:32.030
That doesn't mean it makes sense to have a
crowd of 10000 people in Tulsa, Oklahoma,

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.030
on Saturday.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:36.020
And it certainly doesn't mean that Donald
Trump deserves to be reelected.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:39.510
So my view continues to be.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:48.170
If Trump gets another 12 to 18 months, this
could wind itself down on its own, leaving

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:50.970
untold death in its wake.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:56.790
And you will have Trump ists who will be reinvigorated
and say Trump said it would go away and it

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:57.790
went away.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:58.930
I guess he was sort of right.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:01.230
We can't take any chances on that.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:04.489
Donald Trump needs to be removed in November.

00:04:04.489 --> 00:04:09.550
We have four and a half months until the election
and then it's two and a half more until he

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:14.519
would be replaced with Joe Biden, meaning
in seven months total.

00:04:14.519 --> 00:04:15.519
Right.

00:04:15.519 --> 00:04:19.209
We're talking about January 20, 21st, 20th.

00:04:19.209 --> 00:04:21.690
We could have Trump gone Corona virus.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:22.690
Will it?

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:24.620
In all likelihood, still be a problem at that
point in time.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:29.990
But we could at least start to start to go
back to something that would actually resemble

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.099
sanity at that point in time.

00:04:33.099 --> 00:04:37.539
In terms of the decisions you have to make
over the next two weeks, I would go with Foushee

00:04:37.539 --> 00:04:40.889
over Trump if if you would go with Trump over
Foushee.

00:04:40.889 --> 00:04:42.439
I want to know why.

00:04:42.439 --> 00:04:48.050
If Trump says it's safe to go to a rally with
10000 people and Foushee says it's not, I'm

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.139
going with Foushee.

00:04:49.139 --> 00:04:54.370
I also live in Massachusetts where there are
no rallies of this size taking place.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.159
There are no events of this size taking place.

00:04:56.159 --> 00:04:58.009
And that's a very, very good thing.

